@host = http://localhost:5080
@assessmentKey = poc-key-assessment-001

### 1. Health check (anonymous) - proves the service runs with zero infrastructure
GET {{host}}/health

### 2. Send PasswordReset (happy path - needs SendGrid key + real template id in templates.json)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/email/send
X-Source-System: assessment-portal
X-Api-Key: {{assessmentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "templateKey": "PasswordReset",
  "to": [{ "email": "you@example.org", "name": "Jane" }],
  "data": { "firstName": "Jane", "resetLink": "https://portal/reset?token=demo" },
  "sourceSystem": "assessment-portal"
}

### 3. Auth rejection (no key) - shows per-system auth
POST {{host}}/api/v1/email/send
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "PasswordReset", "to": [{ "email": "you@example.org" }] }

### 4. Unknown template - shows registry governance
POST {{host}}/api/v1/email/send
X-Source-System: assessment-portal
X-Api-Key: {{assessmentKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateKey": "DoesNotExist", "to": [{ "email": "you@example.org" }] }

### 5. Template catalogue - what business users own
GET {{host}}/api/v1/templates
X-Source-System: assessment-portal
X-Api-Key: {{assessmentKey}}

### 6. Indicative preview render
GET {{host}}/api/v1/templates/PasswordReset/preview?data={"firstName":"Jane"}
X-Source-System: assessment-portal
X-Api-Key: {{assessmentKey}}

### 7. Activity audit trail (FR-003 evidence)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/activity?take=20
X-Source-System: assessment-portal
X-Api-Key: {{assessmentKey}}

### 8. Simulated SendGrid event webhook (delivery/open/bounce status updates)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/events/sendgrid
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "event": "delivered", "email": "jane@example.org", "sg_message_id": "demo123" },
  { "event": "open", "email": "jane@example.org", "sg_message_id": "demo123" }
]
